.TH MDGLASS 1 "November 2026" "mdglass 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdglass \- super fast terminal markdown viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdglass
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B mdglass
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdglass
renders markdown with colors, tables, syntax-highlighted code and clickable
links, and shows it in a built-in less-style pager. When standard output is
not a terminal it prints plain text wrapped to 80 columns instead. With no
\fIFILE\fR, or when \fIFILE\fR is \fB\-\fR, it reads standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-export-pdf PATH
Export one Markdown document to a paginated PDF without opening a window.
Requires system Cairo, Pango and PangoCairo libraries; vector diagrams also
use librsvg. No display server, browser or external conversion program is
required. An existing destination is replaced only after successful export.
The input document cannot be used as the destination.
.TP
.B \-\-paper a4|a3|letter|legal
PDF paper size (default a4).
.TP
.B \-\-landscape
Use landscape PDF pages.
.TP
.B \-\-margin PT
PDF margins in points (72 per inch), default 36.
.TP
.B \-\-font-size PT
PDF body font size in points, default 10 (allowed range 4 to 72).
.TP
.B \-\-table-mode auto|fit|tile
Wrap table cells and repeat headers on continuation pages. Auto (default)
uses column bands for tables too wide to fit readably; tile explicitly uses
column bands. Fit requires the table to fit the page width.
Cells are not truncated. Box-drawing tables in code fences remain code.
.TP
.B \-\-diagram-mode auto|fit|tile
Fit diagrams uniformly, or tile oversized diagrams with continuation labels.
Auto is the default. Tile boundaries may cross diagram nodes or labels.
Unsupported diagrams remain source; external renderers are never invoked.
.TP
.B \-\-overlap PT
Diagram tile overlap in points, default 12.
.TP
.B \-\-no-repeat-first-column
Do not repeat the first identifier column in horizontal table bands.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gui
Open a native GNOME preview window (GTK4 + libadwaita) instead of the pager.
Requires the system libraries \fBlibgtk-4\fR and \fBlibadwaita-1\fR, which are
loaded at runtime; no extra packages are needed on a standard Ubuntu desktop.
Prose wraps to the window width; wide tables and code blocks keep their
shape and scroll sideways instead of being broken across lines. The wraps
are real line breaks, as in the terminal: find does not match a phrase split
across two lines, copied text keeps the breaks, and resizing or zooming
clears a selection.
Blocks fenced as \fBmermaid\fR and untyped blocks that look like box art
are drawn as vector pictures, in a palette that follows the light/dark
style; a block that cannot be drawn (no SVG loader,
unparsable input) is shown as its code instead. In the terminal, mermaid
fences are drawn as ASCII box art instead: flowcharts, state machines,
ER models, sequence diagrams and pie charts; syntax that cannot be drawn
truthfully at the terminal width stays code (see \fB\-\-no\-diagrams\fR
and the \fBD\fR key); piped output keeps the markdown source unless
\fB\-\-color\fR forces art.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-pager
Print the rendered output to standard output instead of opening the pager.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-plain
Disable colors. This is the default when standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force colors, for example \fBmdglass \-n \-\-color FILE | less \-R\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-urls
Do not show link URLs after the link text.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-diagrams
Render mermaid fences as their source code instead of ASCII box art.
Box art normally appears only where a human reads it: in the pager, or
in \fB\-n\fR output when colors are on. Combine with \fB\-\-color\fR when
redirecting to a file that should still be searched as source.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS (PAGER)
.TP
.BR j " " k ", " Down " " Up ", " Enter
Scroll one line down / up.
.TP
.BR d " " u ", " Ctrl\-D " " Ctrl\-U
Scroll half a page down / up.
.TP
.BR f " " b ", " Space ", " PgDn " " PgUp
Scroll a page down / up.
.TP
.BR gg " " G ", " Home " " End
Go to the top / bottom.
.TP
.BR / " " ?
Search forward / backward (case-insensitive).
.TP
.BR n " " N
Go to the next / previous match.
.TP
.BR ] " " [
Show the next / previous file.
.TP
.B D
Toggle mermaid fences between box art and source code.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit, or move on to the next file when several were given.
.SH GUI ACTIONS
.BR Ctrl+P
Open the native print dialog. Print and PDF export share a page-layout engine;
screen wrapping and zoom do not affect output. Export as PDF is also available
from the window menu. Both actions offer page-layout settings. PDF export
runs in the background on a document snapshot and can be cancelled; a native
renderer call already in progress must finish before cancellation takes effect.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+O
Open a file (also \fBAlt+Left/Right\fR for previous/next of the files given).
.TP
.BR Ctrl+F
Find bar with live match highlighting; Enter and the arrow buttons cycle
matches, Esc closes.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+R " or " F5
Reload the current file. Files are also reloaded automatically when changed.
.TP
.BR Ctrl++ "/" \- "/ " Ctrl+0
Zoom in, out, reset.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+W
Close the window.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, colors are disabled unless \fB\-\-color\fR is given.
.TP
.B TERM
When \fBdumb\fR, colors are disabled unless \fB\-\-color\fR is given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a file could not be read, output failed or the GUI could not start,
2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mdglass README.md
mdglass a.md b.md
curl \-s https://example.com/notes.md | mdglass
mdglass notes.md | grep TODO
mdglass --gui README.md          # native GNOME preview window
mdglass --export-pdf notes.pdf notes.md
mdglass --export-pdf wide.pdf --landscape --table-mode tile notes.md
.fi
